    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0466" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/368</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-24">September 24, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Yung Kwai, Counselor and Chargé of the Chinese Legation, called to see me
                    today and referred to my conversation with him of September 17. He stated that
                    he had a reply from his Government which he had translated and which he handed
                    to me, which is attached hereto.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d224-f1"/> He said that
                    he was sorry that he could not bring a more favorable response.</p>
                <closer><signed>N[<hi rendition="#small-caps">elson</hi>] T. J[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ohnson</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
